.Dd "ipsec-tools / racoon @RACOON_PACKAGE_VERSION@"
.Dt RACOONCTL 1
.Os
.\"
.Sh NAME
.Nm racoonctl
.Nd control and query a running racoon IKE daemon
.\"
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl dl
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.\"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the tool for operating a running
.Xr racoon 8 :
establishing and tearing down VPN connections, inspecting the current
Security Associations and scheduled events, and reloading the daemon's
configuration.
It is the only supported way to do any of this at runtime;
.Xr racoon 8
itself only reads
.Xr racoon.conf 5
at startup or on
.Dv SIGHUP .
.Pp
With privilege separation
.Pq Ic privsep
active in
.Xr racoon.conf 5 ,
which is this project's recommended default (see the Admin Guide's
Privilege Separation section), racoon itself no longer runs as a single
root process an operator might otherwise reach for directly:
.Nm
talking to the admin socket is the intended, and only, interface for a
non-root operator to drive it.
.Pp
.Nm
talks to
.Xr racoon 8
over a
.Xr unix 4
domain socket (the
.Dq admin socket ,
sometimes called the adminport), configured by the
.Ic adminsock
directive in the
.Ic listen
block of
.Xr racoon.conf 5 .
By default that socket is owned
.Li root:root
mode
.Li 0600 ,
which only root can use.
For any non-root user to run
.Nm ,
three things must all be true:
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Xr racoon.conf 5 Ap s
.Ic listen
block has an active
.Ic adminsock
directive naming a group that user belongs to, e.g.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
adminsock "/var/run/racoon/racoon.sock" "root" "racoon" 0660;
.Ed
.Pp
(both packaged roadwarrior client/server configuration templates ship
this active by default \(em see
.Pa racoon.conf.default Ap s
own header comment for exactly where those templates are installed on
this system).
.It
the directory holding that socket (by default the
.Xr racoon 8
runtime state directory, e.g.
.Pa /run/racoon )
grants that same group traversal access.
.Xr racoon 8
sets this itself on every start, whether started via systemd or
manually \(em nothing needs to be created or fixed up by hand first.
.It
the user is actually a member of that group.
.El
.Pp
See the Admin Guide's Privilege Separation section for the full
filesystem ownership policy this implies, and
.Xr racoon.conf 5 Ap s
.Sx Privilege separation
section for the
.Ic adminsock
directive's full syntax.
.Pp
The following general options are available:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d
Debug mode.
Hexdump admin port messages before sending them.
.It Fl l
Increase verbosity.
Mainly affects
.Ic show-sa .
.It Fl s Ar socket
Connect to
.Ar socket
instead of the compile-time default (see
.Sx FILES
below).
Use this when the admin socket has been moved via
.Ic adminsock
in
.Xr racoon.conf 5 ,
or when driving more than one
.Xr racoon 8
instance from the same host.
.El
.\"
.Pp
The following commands are available:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic reload-config
Tell
.Xr racoon 8
to reload
.Xr racoon.conf 5 ,
equivalent to sending it
.Dv SIGHUP .
Note that under privsep, changes to the
.Ic listen
and
.Ic paths
sections are not picked up by a reload; those require a full restart
(see
.Xr racoon.conf 5 Ap s
.Sx Privilege separation
section).
.It Ic show-schedule
Dump
.Xr racoon 8 Ap s
internal event scheduler queue: pending timer-driven work such as
rekeys, retransmissions, and DPD probes.
Primarily a debugging aid, not something a routine VPN operator needs.
.It Ic show-sa Ar protocol
Dump the current Security Associations matching
.Ar protocol :
.Ic isakmp
(Phase 1),
.Ic esp ,
.Ic ah ,
or
.Ic ipsec
(both ESP and AH).
Use
.Fl l
for more detail per SA.
.It Ic get-cert Oo Ic inet | inet6 Oc Ar src dst
Output the raw certificate that authenticated the Phase 1 SA between
.Ar src
and
.Ar dst .
.It Ic flush-sa Ar protocol
Tear down every Security Association matching
.Ar protocol ,
the same values
.Ic show-sa
accepts.
.It Ic delete-sa Ar saopts
Delete one specific Security Association; see
.Sx Parameter specifications
below for
.Ar saopts .
.It Ic establish-sa Oo Fl w Oc Oo Fl n Ar remoteconf Oc \
Oo Fl u Ar identity Oc Ar saopts
Establish one specific Security Association.
.Fl u Ar identity
supplies the XAuth/Hybrid-auth identity when the matching
.Ic remote
block requires one \(em
.Nm
prompts for the associated password interactively.
.Fl n Ar remoteconf
picks a specific
.Ic remote
block by name when more than one could match.
.Fl w
blocks until the SA is actually established (or fails), instead of
returning as soon as the request is sent.
.It Ic vpn-connect Oo Fl u Ar identity Oc Ar vpn_gateway
Shorthand for
.Ic establish-sa
that establishes an ISAKMP (Phase 1) SA with
.Ar vpn_gateway .
This is the command a roadwarrior client operator runs to connect.
.It Ic vpn-disconnect Ar vpn_gateway
Shorthand for
.Ic delete-sa
that tears down every SA associated with
.Ar vpn_gateway .
This is the command a roadwarrior client operator runs to disconnect.
.It Ic show-event
Stream every event
.Xr racoon 8
reports (SA up/down, Phase 1/2 completion, errors) until interrupted.
Useful for watching a connection attempt live.
.It Ic logout-user Ar login
Delete every SA established on behalf of the XAuth/Hybrid-auth user
.Ar login .
Only available when
.Xr racoon 8
was built with Hybrid auth support
.Pq Fl -enable-hybrid .
.It Ic status Oo Fl v Oc Oo Fl f Ic text | json Oc Oo Fl -format Ns = Ns Ic text | json Oc
Read-only runtime introspection: the current Phase 1 SAs (and, with
.Fl v ,
Phase 2 SAs too) as
.Xr racoon 8
holds them right now \(em negotiated algorithms, identities, XAuth and
mode-config state, DPD/NAT-T status, and (per SA) the
.Ic remote
block configuration that governs it
.Pq Ic anonymous , passive , generate_policy .
.Pp
.Fl f Ic json
(or
.Fl -format Ns = Ns Ic json )
selects the machine-readable JSON rendering instead of the default
human-readable text; both present the same fields; text differs only in
layout.
The JSON rendering carries a top-level
.Ic schema_version
field
.Pq Dq major.minor :
additive changes bump the minor version only, breaking changes bump
major.
SPIs are shown masked
.Pq e.g. Li 0x1234**** ,
never in full.
.Pp
Each
.Ic phase2
entry carries
.Ic phase1_index ,
the parent Phase 1's
.Ic index
string, letting a consumer join the two arrays.
Its
.Ic proposal
also carries
.Ic effective_group :
when PFS was negotiated this equals
.Ic pfs_group ;
otherwise it falls back to the parent Phase 1's
.Ic dh_group ,
since per RFC 2409 \(sc5.5 that is the Diffie-Hellman group actually
securing this tunnel's key material when Quick Mode itself performed no
PFS exchange \(em a
.Ic pfs_group
of
.Ic null
does not mean no group protects the tunnel, only that none was
renegotiated at the Phase 2 level.
.Pp
A
.Ic phase2
entry's
.Ic proposal.encryption_algorithm
names the cipher mode along with the cipher
.Pq e.g. Li AES-CBC , not Li AES ,
and its
.Ic proposal.authentication_algorithm
names the hash variant
.Pq e.g. Li hmac-sha1 , not Li hmac-sha .
CBC is the only cipher mode
.Xr racoon 8
implements, so the mode follows from the negotiated transform alone.
.Ic AH
SAs and the
.Ic NULL
and
.Ic RC4
ESP transforms carry no cipher mode and are named without a suffix.
.Pp
.Ic status
is read-only: unlike every other command above, it never establishes,
tears down, or reloads anything.
It does not, and structurally cannot, explain
.Em why
a past negotiation failed \(em by the time a Phase 1 handle would show
a failure, racoon has already deleted it (see
.Ic show-event
for the corresponding, but reason-less, event notification instead).
.Pp
Example
.Pq Fl v Fl f Ic json
output for one established Phase 1 SA with one Phase 2 SA:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
  "schema_version": "1.1",
  "timestamp": "2026-01-15T10:30:00Z",
  "phase1": [
    {
      "index": "0x1122334455667788...",
      "state": "established",
      "remote_id": "198.51.100.1",
      "local_id": "203.0.113.1",
      "version": "1.0",
      "exchange_mode": "MAIN",
      "proposal": {
        "encryption_algorithm": "AES-CBC",
        "hash_algorithm": "SHA256",
        "authentication_method": "pre-shared key",
        "dh_group": "14",
        "lifetime_time": 28800
      },
      "remote_config": {
        "anonymous": true,
        "passive": true,
        "generate_policy": "unique"
      }
    }
  ],
  "phase2": [
    {
      "index": "0x87654321",
      "phase1_index": "0x1122334455667788...",
      "state": "established",
      "spi_in": "0x1234****",
      "spi_out": "0x8765****",
      "protocol": "ESP",
      "encmode": "Tunnel",
      "selectors": {
        "src": "203.0.113.1/32",
        "dst": "198.51.100.1/32",
        "protocol": "any",
        "src_port": "any",
        "dst_port": "any"
      },
      "proposal": {
        "encryption_algorithm": "AES-CBC",
        "authentication_algorithm": "hmac-sha1",
        "pfs_group": 14,
        "effective_group": 14,
        "lifetime_time": 3600,
        "lifetime_bytes": 0
      },
      "reqid_in": 1,
      "reqid_out": 2,
      "ok": true
    }
  ]
}
.Ed
.El
.Pp
Command shortcuts are available:
.Bl -tag -width XXX -compact -offset indent
.It Ic rc
.Ic reload-config
.It Ic sc
.Ic show-schedule
.It Ic ss
.Ic show-sa
.It Ic gc
.Ic get-cert
.It Ic fs
.Ic flush-sa
.It Ic ds
.Ic delete-sa
.It Ic es
.Ic establish-sa
.It Ic vc
.Ic vpn-connect
.It Ic vd
.Ic vpn-disconnect
.It Ic se
.Ic show-event
.It Ic lu
.Ic logout-user
.It Ic st
.Ic status
.El
.\"
.Ss Parameter specifications
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ar protocol
one of
.Ic isakmp , esp , ah ,
or (for
.Ic show-sa
and
.Ic flush-sa
only)
.Ic ipsec .
.It Ar saopts
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ic isakmp Ar family src dst
.It Brq Ic esp | ah Ar family src/prefixlen/port dst/prefixlen/port ul_proto
.El
.It Ar family
.Ic inet
or
.Ic inet6 .
.It Ar ul_proto
one of
.Ic icmp , tcp , udp , gre ,
or
.Ic any .
.El
.\"
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The command exits with 0 on success, and non-zero on errors.
.\"
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa /var/run/racoon/racoon.sock
default admin socket path on this project's own Debian and Arch
packaging builds (compile-time
.Va ADMINPORTDIR
derived from
.Fl -localstatedir ) .
.It Pa /var/lib/racoon/racoon.sock
default admin socket path on a vanilla upstream build with no
.Fl -localstatedir
override.
.El
.Pp
Run
.Nm
.Fl s Ar /path/to/racoon.sock
if your build uses neither.
.\"
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ipsec 4 ,
.Xr racoon.conf 5 ,
.Xr racoon 8
.\"
.Sh HISTORY
Once was
.Ic kmpstat
in the KAME project.
It turned into
.Nm
but remained undocumented for a while.
.An Emmanuel Dreyfus Aq manu@NetBSD.org
wrote the original version of this man page.
